# Overview

This document walks through the two-part R pipeline that produces the **GEV modelling input table** from PCIC's gridded and station hydrologic model outputs.

- **Part A — `merge_station_coord.R`** combines the ~190 per-station ASCII streamflow files with a coordinate spreadsheet to produce the merged station tables (`stream_coor_station_3_model.csv`, plus per-scenario splits).
- **Part B — gridded baseflow extraction** loads the NetCDF baseflow rasters, builds a **5 × 5 grid neighbourhood** around each station, writes a masked GeoTIFF, and produces a **top-9 daily mean** "representative baseflow" parquet table. Finally it merges that baseflow covariate onto the station yearly-maximum streamflow table.

## Pipeline diagram

```
Station portal CSVs (≈190)         station_coordinate_apr15.xlsx
       │                                       │
       └────────────────┬──────────────────────┘
                        ▼
            merge_station_coord.R               (Part A)
                        │
        ┌───────────────┼───────────────────────────────┐
        ▼               ▼                               ▼
stream_coor_      stream_coor_              stream_coor_station_
station_hist.csv   station_rcp45.csv         rcp85.csv  (+ 3_model.csv)
        │
        │ (coords)
        ▼
Gridded NetCDF (BASEFLOW)  ──►  Gridded baseflow script        (Part B)
                                        │
                  ┌─────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┐
                  ▼                     ▼                           ▼
       daily_bf_<target>.tif   avg_daily_bf_<target>.parquet   sf_yearly_max_<target>.csv
            (Output 1)              (Output 2)                  (already produced upstream)
                                        │                           │
                                        └──────── join (Output 3) ──┘
                                                  │
                                                  ▼
                                         year_<target>_sf_bf.csv
                                         (GEV modelling input)
```

## Target dataset switch

Both scripts are driven by a single character flag — typically one of:

```r
target_dataset <- "history"   # or "rcp45", "rcp85"
```

The downstream filenames (`daily_bf_<target>.tif`, `avg_daily_bf_<target>.parquet`, `year_<target>_sf_bf.csv`) inherit this value, so a single run produces one consistent set of files.

