# Part A — `merge_station_coord.R`

**Goal.** Read every `*.csv.ascii` station streamflow file, keep only the columns needed (PNWNAmet + the chosen CanESM2 runs), attach station coordinates, and write merged tables.

## A.1 — Load coordinates and list station files

```{r merge-load, eval=FALSE}
library(tidyverse)
library(readxl)

# 1. Coordinate file: one row per station with Location Code, Longitude, Latitude
coords_df       <- read_excel("station_coordinate_apr15.xlsx")
coords_stations <- coords_df$`Location Code`
cat("Number of stations in Excel coordinates file:", nrow(coords_df), "\n")

# 2. ASCII station files
file_list     <- list.files("model_flow", pattern = "\\.csv\\.ascii$", full.names = TRUE)
file_stations <- str_extract(basename(file_list), "^[^.]+")
```

## A.2 — Pre-merge diagnostics

Sanity-check that the Excel sheet and the downloaded file set agree before doing any heavy work.

```{r merge-diag, eval=FALSE}
missing_data   <- setdiff(coords_stations, file_stations)  # in xlsx, no CSV
missing_coords <- setdiff(file_stations, coords_stations)  # CSV present, no xlsx row

if (length(missing_data) > 0) {
  cat("WARNING: Stations in Excel but MISSING CSV files:\n"); print(missing_data)
}
if (length(missing_coords) > 0) {
  cat("WARNING: CSV files with no matching coordinate row:\n"); print(missing_coords)
}

valid_stations <- intersect(file_stations, coords_stations)
valid_files    <- file_list[file_stations %in% valid_stations]
```

## A.3 — File inspection (one-off debug)

PCIC's ASCII files start with a "sequence" comment line, so the actual header is on **line 2**. The debug block helps confirm this before batch processing.

```{r merge-debug, eval=FALSE}
sample_file <- valid_files[1]
readLines(sample_file, n = 10)                # confirm row-1 is a junk/sequence line
sample_df <- read_csv(sample_file, show_col_types = FALSE)
print(colnames(sample_df))
print(head(sample_df))
```

## A.4 — Per-station reader

Each station file is reduced to the four useful columns: `Date`, `PNWNAmet` (historical observation-based run), and the two CanESM2 future runs.

```{r merge-fn, eval=FALSE}
process_station <- function(file_path) {
  station_name <- str_extract(basename(file_path), "^[^.]+")

  # skip the "sequence" junk line so line 2 becomes the header
  df <- read_csv(file_path, skip = 1, show_col_types = FALSE)

  df %>%
    select(Date, PNWNAmet, CanESM2_rcp45_r1i1p1, CanESM2_rcp85_r1i1p1) %>%
    mutate(
      Date    = as.Date(Date, format = "%Y/%m/%d"),
      Station = station_name
    )
}
```

## A.5 — Combine + join coordinates + write

```{r merge-combine, eval=FALSE}
cat("Processing", length(valid_files), "valid stations...\n")
all_station_data <- map_dfr(valid_files, process_station)

final_merged_data <- all_station_data %>%
  inner_join(coords_df, by = c("Station" = "Location Code")) %>%
  relocate(Station, Longitude, Latitude)

write_csv(final_merged_data, "stream_coor_station_3_model.csv")
```

## A.6 — Split into per-scenario files

The full merged file is heavy because it carries three streamflow columns. Splitting into three slim files makes the downstream web app / GEV step lighter.

```{r merge-split, eval=FALSE}
stream_coor_station_3_model <- read_csv("stream_coor_station_3_model.csv")

# Historical (PNWNAmet observation-based)
stream_coor_station_3_model %>%
  select(Station, Longitude, Latitude, Date, PNWNAmet) %>%
  write_csv("stream_coor_station_hist.csv")

# CanESM2 RCP 4.5
stream_coor_station_3_model %>%
  select(Station, Longitude, Latitude, Date, CanESM2_rcp45_r1i1p1) %>%
  write_csv("stream_coor_station_rcp45.csv")

# CanESM2 RCP 8.5
stream_coor_station_3_model %>%
  select(Station, Longitude, Latitude, Date, CanESM2_rcp85_r1i1p1) %>%
  write_csv("stream_coor_station_rcp85.csv")
```

## A.7 — Date-value mismatch check

Quick QC: on overlapping historical years the PNWNAmet column and the GCM-historical period should *not* be identical (they're different forcings), so a high mismatch count is expected and reassuring.

```{r merge-check, eval=FALSE}
date_mismatch_hist_rcp45 <- stream_coor_station_3_model %>%
  filter(PNWNAmet != CanESM2_rcp45_r1i1p1) %>%
  summarise(count = n())

total_rows <- nrow(stream_coor_station_3_model)
cat("Mismatched rows hist vs rcp45:", date_mismatch_hist_rcp45$count, "\n")
cat("Proportion:", date_mismatch_hist_rcp45$count / total_rows, "\n")
```

